 "expected": {
  "TestConcat": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "reason": "divergence: it counts allocations with testing.AllocsPerRun, and gocpp allocates differently than Go (it counts C++ operator new; append(s, make(S, n)...) and string(bytes) allocate a temporary); counting rule of the Phase 09 README, 2.8"
  },
  "TestConcat_too_large": {
   "class": "bug",
   "reason": "bug: it makes a slice of zero-size elements (struct{}) with a length up to math.MaxInt, and gocpp slices cost one byte for each element (the C++ size of an empty struct is 1), so makeslice panics with len out of range; Go allocates nothing"
  },
  "TestGrow": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "reason": "divergence: it counts allocations with testing.AllocsPerRun, and gocpp allocates differently than Go (it counts C++ operator new; append(s, make(S, n)...) and string(bytes) allocate a temporary); counting rule of the Phase 09 README, 2.8"
  },
  "TestInsert": {
   "class": "divergence",
   "reason": "divergence: it counts allocations with testing.AllocsPerRun, and gocpp allocates differently than Go (it counts C++ operator new; append(s, make(S, n)...) and string(bytes) allocate a temporary); counting rule of the Phase 09 README, 2.8"
  },
  "TestRepeat": {
   "class": "bug",
   "reason": "bug: it makes a slice of zero-size elements (struct{}) with a length up to math.MaxInt, and gocpp slices cost one byte for each element (the C++ size of an empty struct is 1), so makeslice panics with len out of range; Go allocates nothing"
  }
